tabs.c by Robert A. LarsonThis program can be used to:	convert from one tab size to another	optimize spacing/tabbing to a minimum number of characters	replace tabs with spaces	replace spaces with tabs	delete trailing spaces/tabs on linesIt is used as a filter, input is from standard input and output is tostandard output.Options:	-iNN	Tabs on the input file are set every NN spaces.		(Default 8)  If NN is 0 or omited, input tabs are not		treated as special characters.	(Probably only useful		with -o0 and -t)	-oNN	Tabs on the output file are set every NN spaces.		(Default 8)  If NN is 0 or omited, tabs are not used		in the output file.	-t	Suppress trailing spaces/tabs from output lines.	-q	don't process in quotesOptions may be specified separatly or together.  Spaces are not allowedbetween the i or o option and the number following.This program will always eliminate reduntant spaceing.  If this is allthat is desired, set the input and output tab size identicly.Use:	tabs -i8 -o8 <infile >outfile		Optimize out extra spaces, normal tab stops.	tabs -i4t <infile >outfile		Convert from Microware's silly 4 character tabs to normal		8 character tabs and eliminate trailing spaces.	tabs -q -t <infile >outfile		Optimize out extra spaces from C source without messing		up quoted strings.